1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,622
Three charts. Three new skills to test.

2
00:00:02,991 --> 00:00:04,563
Traps, tops and targets.

3
00:00:05,063 --> 00:00:07,815
Question one. Price just dipped below support.

4
00:00:08,163 --> 00:00:10,533
Is this a real breakdown, or a bear trap?

5
00:00:14,383 --> 00:00:15,195
A bear trap.

6
00:00:15,603 --> 00:00:22,698
The dip came on thin volume, then buyers snapped it straight back above support. Sellers who shorted the break got caught.

7
00:00:23,198 --> 00:00:27,883
Question two. Price has hit the same high twice, and it's starting to roll over.

8
00:00:28,222 --> 00:00:31,750
What's the pattern? A double top, a bull flag, or a triangle?

9
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,526
A double top.

10
00:00:36,920 --> 00:00:44,161
Two failed pushes at the same high, then the neckline broke. Until that neckline breaks, it's only a possible double top.

11
00:00:44,661 --> 00:00:47,552
Question three. You bought near the bottom of the range.

12
00:00:47,926 --> 00:00:50,632
Where does your take-profit go? A, B, or C?

13
00:00:54,482 --> 00:00:56,506
A, just below the old resistance.

14
00:00:56,843 --> 00:01:03,193
C cuts a good trade short, and B sits beyond a level that's turned price away before, so it may never fill.

15
00:01:03,693 --> 00:01:06,437
How many did you get? Tell me your score in the comments.

16
00:01:06,828 --> 00:01:10,460
Practise on real charts from the game, at memestreet.net.

